Along those lines, I'd expect the monsters to use some of the other
items too - liches that read enchant armor/weapon scrolls - and
improvements in their AI. They could bounce rays off walls to hit
you, but avoid hitting each other, at least when lawful.

Probably, some future version, though not the next one, will include
class levels for monsters working much like those for players. Like us,
the monsters would also have skills with the weapons and spell-schools

This makes the monsters potentially more dangerous while reusing
large chunks of existing code. While you can give liches the
equivalent of expert skill in attack spells with special case code
that's not a very flexible approach.


